---
import SolutionPage from '../../../layouts/SolutionPage.astro';
---

<SolutionPage
  title="Light Environment"
  parent="Mitigate"
  oneliner="The light entering your eyes controls your hormones, your sleep, and your energy — and most indoor light is wrong."
  slug="environment-light"
  canonicalPath="/solutions/environment/light"
  showSolutionPath={false}
  showDisclaimer={false}
>
  <!-- ── Why This Matters ── -->
  <h2>Why This Matters</h2>
  <ul class="insult-list">
    <li>Light spectrum, timing, and intensity dictates melatonin production, cortisol curves, testosterone release timing, and metabolic rate throughout the day</li>
    <li>Standard LED and fluorescent bulbs emit a blue-dominant spectrum that tells your brain it's high noon — at 10pm — suppressing melatonin and degrading sleep architecture</li>
    <li>Most men indoors all morning never get the full-spectrum sunlight that anchors the circadian clock — the result is a system running with no strong signal at either end</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- ── Featured Products — E-Commerce Hero ── -->
  <h2 class="section-eliminate">Featured Products</h2>
  <p>Protocol-matched products for your light environment. Affiliate relationships disclosed below.</p>
  <div class="product-grid">
    <div class="product-card">
      <h3>Circadian-Friendly LED Bulbs</h3>
      <p class="product-why">Minimizes blue-light output in evening hours to protect melatonin production.</p>
      <p>Warm-spectrum (2200K) LED replacement bulbs for bedroom and living areas.</p>
      <span class="notify-pill">Notify Me When Available</span>
