    </div>
    <div class="product-card">
      <h3>Blue-Light Blocking Glasses</h3>
      <p class="product-why">Blocks 90%+ of blue-spectrum from screens and overhead lighting after sundown.</p>
      <p>Amber-lens frames for evening wear — no change to screen habits required.</p>
      <span class="notify-pill">Notify Me When Available</span>
      <!-- TODO: wire to Stripe Checkout when shop is live — /api/checkout?sku=blue-blocker-glasses -->
      <a href="mailto:hello@my4mlife.com?subject=Pre-order: Blue-Light Blocking Glasses" class="btn-cart">Notify Me →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="product-card">
      <h3>Red-Light Therapy Panel</h3>
      <p class="product-why">Supports mitochondrial function, tissue recovery, and mood via 660nm / 850nm wavelengths.</p>
      <p>Full-size panel for whole-body red and near-infrared light therapy sessions (10–20 min/day).</p>
      <span class="notify-pill">Notify Me When Available</span>
      <!-- TODO: wire to Stripe Checkout when shop is live — /api/checkout?sku=red-light-panel -->
      <a href="mailto:hello@my4mlife.com?subject=Pre-order: Red-Light Therapy Panel" class="btn-cart">Notify Me →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="product-card">
      <h3>Full-Spectrum Morning Lamp</h3>
      <p class="product-why">Anchors circadian rhythm for indoor workers and northern-latitude users without reliable morning sun.</p>
      <p>10,000 lux full-spectrum lamp — 10 min exposure on waking replaces outdoor morning light.</p>
      <span class="notify-pill">Notify Me When Available</span>
      <!-- TODO: wire to Stripe Checkout when shop is live — /api/checkout?sku=morning-lamp -->
      <a href="mailto:hello@my4mlife.com?subject=Pre-order: Full-Spectrum Morning Lamp" class="btn-cart">Notify Me →</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── Deeper Protocol ── -->
  <h2>The Deeper Protocol</h2>
  <ul class="insult-list">
    <li>Blue-spectrum LED bulbs in the bedroom and living room active all evening</li>
    <li>No direct morning sun within 30 minutes of waking — the primary circadian anchor</li>
    <li>Screens within 60 minutes of sleep — melatonin suppression at the worst possible time</li>
    <li>Sunglasses during the first 30 minutes after waking — blocks the signal before it reaches the suprachiasmatic nucleus</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Fix sequence: morning sun first (free, immediate, highest leverage) → swap evening bulbs to warm-spectrum →
    add blue-blockers for screens after sundown → layer in red-light therapy for mitochondrial support.
    Each step compounds the one before it.
  </p>

